An individual who sat in the box.

00:35:47.660 --> 00:35:49.121
I don't need to listen to the evidence.

00:35:49.141 --> 00:35:50.181
I'll just sit here and

00:35:51.702 --> 00:35:52.683
I won't get found guilty.

00:35:55.224 --> 00:36:00.107
And glancing across at the jury members and seeing them looking at him and shaking their head and as if to say,

00:36:00.287 --> 00:36:00.988
what's he doing?

00:36:01.968 --> 00:36:04.370
But then the artwork is produced.

00:36:05.930 --> 00:36:07.211
You could see he was uneasy.

00:36:07.271 --> 00:36:08.492
He would shirk his shoulders.

00:36:08.493 --> 00:36:08.772
In fact,

00:36:08.792 --> 00:36:13.295
a couple of times he just closed his eyes and just bowed his head and you're wondering whether he was half asleep.

00:36:14.936 --> 00:36:15.696
When we produced...

00:36:16.124 --> 00:36:18.350
Some of those artwork and some of those verses,

00:36:19.031 --> 00:36:20.996
he knew that the wars were closing in on him.

00:36:26.088 --> 00:36:29.150
He was questioned about a series of his drawings and poems.

00:36:29.350 --> 00:36:32.272
They revealed a hatred of women and an obsession with murder.

00:36:32.733 --> 00:36:34.794
In one picture there was a gravestone and the words

00:36:35.134 --> 00:36:36.775
R.I.P. Melissa Halstead.

00:36:37.336 --> 00:36:38.476
In another poem he wrote,

00:36:38.657 --> 00:36:39.517
poor old Melissa,

00:36:39.958 --> 00:36:41.078
chopped her up in bits,

00:36:41.459 --> 00:36:42.579
food to feed the fish.

00:36:43.140 --> 00:36:45.842
A further image of a man with an axe was entitled,

00:36:46.222 --> 00:36:48.643
A Romantic Weekend for Two in Austria.

00:36:49.404 --> 00:36:52.266
The court heard from her sister via video link from America,

00:36:52.766 --> 00:36:55.108
who claimed Melissa had predicted her own death.

00:36:55.508 --> 00:36:56.809
Saying if she ever went missing,

00:36:57.189 --> 00:36:58.650
John Sweeney would have killed her.

00:37:00.672 --> 00:37:02.673
As far as the deliberations is concerned,

00:37:03.134 --> 00:37:08.398
that took about three to four days for the jury to decide whether or not he was guilty.

00:37:12.280 --> 00:37:16.203
They would have to have gone all the way back to the relationship with Melissa,

00:37:16.463 --> 00:37:18.885
dating back as far as 1986.

00:37:22.088 --> 00:37:22.608
Events with...

00:37:22.728 --> 00:37:27.813
Delia between 1990 and 1994 with the murder of Paula Fields.

00:37:29.774 --> 00:37:34.839
And then the investigation that takes place up to 2010 before he's arrested again.

00:37:37.001 --> 00:37:38.102
So four days'

00:37:38.562 --> 00:37:40.664
deliberation in the scheme of things was,

00:37:41.605 --> 00:37:41.865
you know,

00:37:42.045 --> 00:37:44.888
quite quick when you consider the amount of evidence they had to go through.

00:37:54.752 --> 00:37:55.953
And then the verdict was given.

00:37:57.113 --> 00:37:58.134
The jury came out and said,

00:37:58.194 --> 00:37:58.674
unanimous,

00:37:59.815 --> 00:38:00.835
guilty on both counts.

00:38:03.077 --> 00:38:06.498
A carpenter has been found guilty of murdering two former girlfriends,

00:38:06.558 --> 00:38:08.259
Melissa Halstead and Paula Fields,

00:38:08.599 --> 00:38:10.921
and throwing their mutilated bodies in canals.

00:38:11.221 --> 00:38:13.722
Although Sweeney showed no emotion in court,

00:38:13.742 --> 00:38:15.363
the family of Paula Fields,

00:38:15.364 --> 00:38:16.484
who were in the public gallery,

00:38:16.584 --> 00:38:19.225
could be heard crying when they heard those verdicts.

00:38:21.987 --> 00:38:24.048
There was always a temptation to...

00:38:24.856 --> 00:38:26.778
Look in his direction as if to say,

00:38:27.238 --> 00:38:27.859
we got you.

00:38:27.959 --> 00:38:30.702
But my contact would have been with the family who were sitting in the gallery.

00:38:31.342 --> 00:38:33.144
What it has meant to lose Paula,

00:38:33.644 --> 00:38:35.586
no one will ever know or understand.

00:38:36.447 --> 00:38:42.352
She has suffered this terrible thing and we know she is never coming back and we never said goodbye.

00:38:43.293 --> 00:38:50.440
We hope to God that John Sweeney will never be released for him to do and to another person what he did to Paula.

00:38:51.532 --> 00:39:00.037
Detective Howard Groves believes that John Sweeney's confessional drawings and writings played a key role in securing the guilty verdict.

00:39:03.419 --> 00:39:04.660
If he hadn't done those artwork,

00:39:05.080 --> 00:39:06.481
if he hadn't done those verses,

00:39:07.141 --> 00:39:08.502
he probably wouldn't have been convicted.

00:39:10.664 --> 00:39:16.407
No sane juror would sit in the box and listen to that evidence and actually say he is innocent.

00:39:16.547 --> 00:39:17.748
That just was not going to happen.

00:39:22.136 --> 00:39:25.057
Some people just have a diary every day and write in it what they do,

00:39:25.457 --> 00:39:26.278
and that's innocent.

00:39:27.338 --> 00:39:28.739
He's just taken it to another extreme.

00:39:32.060 --> 00:39:33.521
Some people are quite arrogant,

00:39:34.061 --> 00:39:35.342
and in Sweeney's case he is.

00:39:38.323 --> 00:39:45.406
What is it that drove him to carry on doing all the artwork on verses when there was a slight chance of being found?

00:39:45.566 --> 00:39:47.827
I think it shows a degree of arrogance on his part.

00:39:48.387 --> 00:39:50.408
He obviously assumed that the police officers...

00:39:51.092 --> 00:39:54.654
Myself and others included wouldn't be able to prove it.

00:39:57.735 --> 00:40:00.636
And although it was a demanding and taxing case,

00:40:01.236 --> 00:40:04.438
it was satisfying at the end of the day that he was convicted.

00:40:14.242 --> 00:40:18.644
Delia Barmer endured three years of torment at the hands of John Sweeney.

00:40:20.948 --> 00:40:22.568
After I was mutilated,

00:40:22.869 --> 00:40:23.489
I died.

00:40:23.889 --> 00:40:26.250
That's the only way I can think of myself.

00:40:27.370 --> 00:40:28.910
I don't consider this to be me.

00:40:29.570 --> 00:40:31.691
I want to remember me as I was.

00:40:32.191 --> 00:40:34.092
I want to be who I was,

00:40:34.252 --> 00:40:34.872
not this.

00:40:40.754 --> 00:40:46.335
John Sweeney drew the picture called The Skull Hunter with the axe in his belt.

00:40:47.456 --> 00:40:48.316
He has...

00:40:48.980 --> 00:40:52.742
My scalp or my long blonde hair and hanging near it.

00:40:56.563 --> 00:40:58.344
He had meant to take my scalp.

00:40:58.604 --> 00:40:59.745
That's what he wanted to do.

00:41:01.285 --> 00:41:02.186
Some way kill me,

00:41:02.506 --> 00:41:02.946
properly.

00:41:04.167 --> 00:41:05.667
He didn't quite get that far.

00:41:07.168 --> 00:41:07.708
And he,

00:41:08.108 --> 00:41:09.169
that was his souvenir,

00:41:10.589 --> 00:41:11.950
drawing things like this.

00:41:14.091 --> 00:41:15.992
He wanted whatever he could get.

00:41:21.036 --> 00:41:27.120
Detective Howard Groves will never forget the case that began with a telephone call from Holland.

00:41:28.180 --> 00:41:28.420
You know,

00:41:28.500 --> 00:41:33.323
it's traumatic for the family to have known that their loved ones were killed in a particular manner.

00:41:33.563 --> 00:41:34.524
And that is something that,

00:41:35.084 --> 00:41:35.805
even to this day,

00:41:36.025 --> 00:41:36.285
you know,

00:41:36.305 --> 00:41:38.666
we wish we were in a position where we could say to them,

00:41:38.866 --> 00:41:43.809
we have found all those remains and they can be buried and they can find some solace in that.

00:41:46.951 --> 00:41:47.071
The

00:41:47.652 --> 00:41:47.952
Dutch...

00:41:48.464 --> 00:41:51.007
The cold case team were looking at those cold cases.

00:41:51.887 --> 00:41:52.969
That was a little bit of luck,

00:41:53.789 --> 00:41:55.671
but sometimes you have to make the most of your luck.

00:41:59.755 --> 00:42:06.022
You get on with that gruesome task of finding who's the perpetrator and then hopefully they get convicted.

00:42:06.242 --> 00:42:06.962
And in this case,

00:42:07.383 --> 00:42:08.384
that happened with John Sweeney.

